TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Confirmed that checkpoint cp-weights failed because its fixed command mutates tracked files instead of validating the prepared base. scripts/stage-weights-both.sh computes RECEIPTS=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\" and writes results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json (via scripts/stage-weights.sh) and results/receipts/weights-worker.json (via scp from the worker), both of which are tracked at baseRev 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa; the captured diff shows exactly those two paths dirty with only ts and data.bytes changing (185563801379 -> 185563854698, shards 131 on both nodes), so the staging work itself succeeded while the worktree came back modified. That is why the underlying gate node for cp-weights recorded verdict pass with exitCode 0 yet the run was rejected at stage checkpoint:record with 'spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base'. The result-schema-mismatch / result-projection-timeout detail (finalMessage not projected within 10000 ms for adapter spec-build-driver, exitEvidencePassed false) is the downstream consequence of that rejection aborting the adapter before it emitted its final message, not an independent machinery or session fault, so transient does not apply. Retry also does not apply: cp-weights is kind checkpoint, checkpoint tasks never retry, and the corrective change lies in scripts/stage-weights-both.sh and scripts/stage-weights.sh, outside any authorized implementation path for this checkpoint. The checkpoint must be made read-only with respect to the repository: emit fresh receipts to a run-scoped location outside the worktree (or an ignored path) and compare them against the committed baselines in results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json, failing when status is not pass or the shard count diverges, while tolerating benign byte drift.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/stage-weights-both.sh","scripts/stage-weights.sh"],"goal":"Make the cp-weights checkpoint validate the prepared base without writing to tracked files. Change scripts/stage-weights-both.sh so both node receipts are produced into a run-scoped scratch directory outside the repository worktree (for example a mktemp -d, or a directory supplied via an environment variable with a temp-dir default) instead of into results/receipts/ directly. The script must then compare the freshly collected coordinator and worker receipts against the committed baselines results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json: fail when either receipt has status other than pass, fail when either shard count differs from the committed baseline, and tolerate drift in the ts field and in data.bytes (report the delta rather than failing on it, or bound it with an explicit documented tolerance). Preserve the existing behaviour of streaming scripts/stage-weights.sh to the worker over ssh and collecting its receipt with scp, keep the human-readable per-host summary lines and the final 'both nodes staged' line, and keep set -euo pipefail. After a successful run, git status --porcelain must be empty: no tracked file under results/receipts/ may be modified and no untracked file may be left inside the worktree. Refreshing the committed baselines must be an explicit separate action, not a side effect of running the checkpoint.","acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"checkpoint-leaves-worktree-clean","description":"Running the checkpoint command leaves the git worktree completely clean: no modified tracked files and no new untracked files anywhere in the repository.","argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\""]},{"id":"receipts-not-rewritten","description":"The committed receipt baselines results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json are unchanged after the checkpoint command runs.","argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh >/dev/null && git diff --exit-code -- results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json results/receipts/weights-worker.json"]},{"id":"validation-still-reports-both-nodes","description":"The checkpoint still stages on both nodes and reports success, printing the coordinator and worker summaries and the final 'both nodes staged' line.","argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/stage-weights-both.sh | tee /dev/stderr | grep -q 'both nodes staged'"]},{"id":"no-tracked-receipt-writes-in-source","description":"The script no longer targets the tracked results/receipts directory as its write destination; receipts are collected into a scratch directory outside the worktree.","argv":["bash","-c","! grep -nE 'RECEIPTS=\"?\\$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"]},{"id":"status-mismatch-is-fatal","description":"A receipt whose status is not pass, or whose shard count diverges from the committed baseline, causes the checkpoint to exit non-zero rather than silently succeeding.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -qE 'status.*pass' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh && grep -q 'shards' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"]}],"dependencies":[]}}
